---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { projectRelationships } from '../../../exercises/relationships';
import { loadSources, root } from '../../../scripts/sources';
const { need, requirement, scenario, manifest } = loadSources();
const records = [
  { id: need.id, kind: 'Intent: operational need', path: 'engineering/needs/NEED-001.yaml' },
  { id: requirement.id, kind: 'Definition: proposed system requirement', path: 'engineering/requirements/REQ-COV-001.yaml' },
  { id: scenario.id, kind: 'Definition: reference inputs', path: 'engineering/scenarios/SCN-001.yaml' },
  { id: manifest.model.id, kind: 'Definition: executable model', path: manifest.model.source },
  { id: manifest.test.id, kind: 'Definition: verification test', path: manifest.test.source },
];
const relationships = projectRelationships({ need, requirement, scenario, manifest });
const sources = records.map(record => ({ ...record, text: readFileSync(resolve(root, record.path), 'utf8') }));
---
<Layout title="Engineering sources and traceability">
  <p class="eyebrow">Reference / source traceability</p>
  <h1>Follow the engineering sources.</h1>
  <p>These source views are bundled from the canonical repository files when the site builds. Editing controls in the lab does not alter them.</p>
  <p>For change-impact reasoning, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/03-digital-threads/`}>return to Chapter 3</a>.</p>
  <p>For numerical method and reproduction, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/04-executable-models/`}>return to Chapter 4</a>.</p>
  <p>For controlled configuration comparisons, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/05-experimentation/`}>return to Chapter 5</a>.</p>
  <p>For test execution and evidence interpretation, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/06-verification-evidence/`}>return to Chapter 6</a>.</p>
  <p>For bounded task contracts and proposal review, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/07-agentic-engineering/`}>return to Chapter 7</a>.</p>
  <p>For source context and action authority, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/08-engineering-context/`}>return to Chapter 8</a>.</p>
  <p>For automated feedback and evidence applicability, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/09-continuous-engineering/`}>return to Chapter 9</a>.</p>
  <p>For bounded claims, evidence gaps and review responsibility, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/10-governance-assurance/`}>return to Chapter 10</a>.</p>
  <p>For configurations and evidence reuse, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/11-engineering-knowledge/`}>return to Chapter 11</a>.</p>
  <h2>Intent → definition → evidence</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a href={`#${need.id}`}>{need.id}</a> is the source need of <a href={`#${requirement.id}`}>{requirement.id}</a>.</li>
    <li>The requirement is evaluated under <a href={`#${scenario.id}`}>{scenario.id}</a> using <a href={`#${manifest.model.id}`}>{manifest.model.id}</a>.</li>
    <li><a href={`#${manifest.test.id}`}>{manifest.test.id}</a> evaluates that reference configuration against the requirement’s threshold.</li>
    <li>An evidence execution creates a <code>RESULT-*</code> record with the inputs, result, model version, source commit and run context. The <a href="https://github.com/And-Gu/executable-engineering-lab/actions/workflows/validate.yml">validation workflow</a> retains these as downloadable CI artifacts for 30 days. No saved CI result is displayed here.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>These are different relationships, not a general-purpose knowledge graph. A browser what-if run is temporary, and a changed configuration is no longer the unmodified reference scenario.</p>
  <section id="relationships">
    <h2>Read the relationship roles</h2>
    <p>These rows come from the canonical fields. Identity and relationship roles are distinct from the revision of each definition.</p>
    <div class="relationship-table" role="region" aria-label="Canonical relationship roles" tabindex="0"><table><caption>Existing source fields and their meanings</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">Target</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>{relationships.map(link => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={`#${link.from}`}>{link.from}</a></th><td><code>{link.field}</code></td><td><a href={`#${link.to}`}>{link.to}</a></td><td>{link.meaning}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/02-engineering-information-models/#contracts`}>Return to Chapter 2’s validation checks</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="proposal-evidence">
    <h2>Proposal analysis is a different record</h2>
    <p>The same validation runs retain a separate <code>proposal-analysis-&lt;commit&gt;</code> artifact. Download a chosen revision’s JSON and inspect <code>definition.baseline</code>, <code>definition.proposed</code>, <code>differences</code>, calculation and execution context. Its kind is <code>unapproved-proposal-analysis</code> and <code>verification.testExecuted</code> is false: it does not claim TEST-COV-001 verified the proposal.</p>
    <p>These artifacts also expire after 30 days and may require GitHub sign-in. Reproduce them at the intended revision with <code>npm ci</code>, <code>npm run check</code> and <code>npm run proposals</code>. Browser proposals never create these retained records.</p>
    <p><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/02-engineering-information-models/#evidence`}>Return to Chapter 2’s evidence interpretation</a> · <a href="https://github.com/And-Gu/executable-engineering-lab/blob/main/docs/02-proposal-exercise.md">Repository exercise</a></p>
  </section>
  <section id="retained-evidence">
    <h2>Inspect a retained reference evaluation record</h2>
    <p><code>npm run evidence</code> calculates and evaluates canonical inputs; it does not itself invoke Vitest. The record’s test ID associates the registered reference context. Inspect the separate test command and workflow logs to establish assertion execution. <a href="https://github.com/And-Gu/executable-engineering-lab/blob/main/docs/06-evidence-review.md">Reproduce and review both activities</a>.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the <a href="https://github.com/And-Gu/executable-engineering-lab/actions/workflows/validate.yml?query=branch%3Amain">main-branch validation runs</a> and select a successful run for the revision you want to inspect.</li>
      <li>Download its <code>reference-evidence-&lt;commit&gt;</code> artifact (GitHub sign-in may be required). Artifacts expire after 30 days.</li>
      <li>Open <code>reference-evidence.json</code>. Check <code>execution.sourceCommit</code>, <code>runTimestamp</code>, <code>workingTreeDirty</code> and <code>context</code> before interpreting <code>definition</code> and <code>calculation</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The record includes exact inputs, model version, sampling method/resolution, threshold, result and requirement outcome. No live “latest PASS” is implied by this page. If an artifact has expired, reproduce a local record with <code>npm ci</code>, <code>npm test</code> and <code>npm run evidence</code> at the intended source revision; that new run has its own timestamp and context.</p>
    <p><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}learn/01-engineering-intent/#evidence`}>Return to interpreting evidence</a> · <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}lab/`}>Explore a temporary browser configuration</a></p>
  </section>
  {sources.map(source => <section id={source.id}>
    <h2>{source.id}</h2><p>{source.kind} · <code>{source.path}</code></p>
    <pre tabindex="0" aria-label={`${source.id} source`}><code>{source.text}</code></pre>
  </section>)}
  <h2>Model and test registration</h2>
  <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Model and test manifest"><code>{readFileSync(resolve(root, 'engineering/manifest.yaml'), 'utf8')}</code></pre>
  <h2>Evaluation rule</h2>
  <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Threshold evaluator source"><code>{readFileSync(resolve(root, 'models/coverage/evaluate.ts'), 'utf8')}</code></pre>
</Layout>
<style>
  section { scroll-margin-top: 1rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
  pre { max-width: 100%; overflow: auto; padding: 1rem; background: var(--surface-muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  .relationship-table { overflow: auto; max-width: 100%; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; background: var(--surface); }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--sage-olive); padding: .7rem; text-align: left; }
  caption { text-align: left; margin: .6rem 0; }
  .relationship-table:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--dusty-violet); outline-offset: 3px; }
  pre code { padding: 0; }
  pre:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--dusty-violet); outline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
